    },
    {
      "color" : "2",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "1fbec7f01c35e01c",
      "text" : "ministerial\n\n1. adj. 部长的；内阁的；公使的；牧师的\n\n--- AI 释义 ---\n1）英\/ ˌmɪnɪˈstɪəriəl \/  美\/ ˌmɪnɪˈstɪriəl \/\n2）\nadj.部长的，大臣的；行政性的，执行性的；（神学）牧师的，神职的\n3）relating to or involving a government minister or the ministry; also used to describe tasks or duties that are clerical or administrative in nature, often without requiring independent judgment\n4）The commission were ministerial details, and failing to carry them out did not imply any substantive decision.",
      "type" : "text",
      "width" : 260,
      "x" : 3396,
      "y" : 3720
    },
    {
      "color" : "2",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "042f6f87dc1f324c",
      "text" : "inadvertence\n*inadvertences*\n\n1. n. 不注意；怠慢，疏忽\n\n--- AI 释义 ---\n1）英\/ ˌɪnədˈvɜːtəns \/  美\/ ˌɪnədˈvɜːrtəns \/\n2）n.疏忽，不经心；无意之举\n3）the fact of being unintentional or resulting from lack of attention; an oversight or mistake made carelessly\n4）Through inadvertence, a few commissions were not delivered to the new officeholders.",
      "type" : "text",
      "width" : 260,
      "x" : 3124,
      "y" : 3324
    },
    {
      "color" : "1",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "446a1a0015cedc60",
      "text" : "mandamus\n*mandamuss*\n\n1. n. 命令书；书面训令\n2. vt. 发训令（过去式mandamused，过去分词mandamused，现在分词mandamusing，第三人称单数mandamuses）\n\n--- AI 释义 ---\n1）英\/ mænˈdeɪməs \/  美\/ mænˈdeɪməs \/\n2）\nn.（法律）执行职务令，命令状（上级法院向下级法院、官员或机构发出的履行法定职责的命令）\n3）a judicial writ issued as a command to an inferior court, public official, or corporation to perform a specified act that is required by law as part of their duty\n4）The party sought a writ of mandamus in the Supreme Court to compel the lower court to hear the case.",
      "type" : "text",
      "width" : 260,
      "x" : 3124,
      "y" : 3456
    },
    {
      "color" : "2",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "9072dcea670c4484",
      "text" : "ceded\n*cede*\n\n1. vt. 屈服；让与；割让（cede的过去式）",
