    },
    {
      "color" : "5",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "9845ae962d7d5c47",
      "text" : "syllogism\n*syllogisms*\n\n1. n. 三段论；推论\n\n--- AI 释义 ---\n1）英\/ˈsɪlədʒɪzəm\/ 美\/ˈsɪlədʒɪzəm\/\n2）n.三段论，演绎推理\n3）a deductive scheme of a formal argument consisting of a major and a minor premise and a conclusion\n4）Thus Marshall neatly concludes the syllogism.",
      "type" : "text",
      "width" : 260,
      "x" : 3396,
      "y" : 3852
    },
    {
      "color" : "4",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "4ce96796fc37fb16",
      "text" : "acquiescing\n*acquiesce, acquiescings*\n\n1. v. 默认，默许( acquiesce的现在分词 )\n\n--- AI 释义 ---\n1）英\/ ˌækwiˈesɪŋ \/ 美\/ ˌækwiˈesɪŋ \/\n2）v.默许，默认，顺从，勉强同意\n3）to accept something without protest, but often without enthusiasm or agreement\n4）He would be acquiescing in an assumption of power by the executive.",
      "type" : "text",
      "width" : 260,
      "x" : 3124,
      "y" : 3588
    },
    {
      "color" : "2",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "71c286f9f4c3b208",
      "text" : "sidestep\n*sidestepped, sidestepping, sidesteps*\n\n1. n. 台阶；横跨的一步\n2. vt. 回避；横跨一步躲避\n3. vi. 回避问题；侧向跨步\n\n--- AI 释义 ---\n1）英\/ ˈsaɪdstep \/  美\/ ˈsaɪdstep \/\n2）v.回避，避开；侧步避开\n3）to avoid dealing with something, especially a difficult or controversial issue, by not addressing it directly\n4）The chief justice sought to sidestep the controversy by claiming the power of judicial review for the Court but exercising it in a way that denied Marbury his commission.",
      "type" : "text",
      "width" : 260,
      "x" : 3124,
      "y" : 3720
    },
    {
      "color" : "3",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "c7cd653f24814486",
