      "y" : 2532
    },
    {
      "color" : "1",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "fbce45c669d2e1df",
      "text" : "delegated\n*delegate*\n\n1. v. 授权（delegate的过去分词）；委托；派…代表\n\n--- AI 释义 ---\n1）英\/ˈdelɪɡeɪtɪd\/  美\/ˈdeləɡeɪtɪd\/\n2）v.授权，委托；委派……为代表\n3）to give someone else a particular job, duty, or right to act on your behalf\n4）On behalf of the people, delegated powers to the federal government.",
      "type" : "text",
      "width" : 260,
      "x" : 3124,
      "y" : 2004
    },
    {
      "color" : "2",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "cfdd3f54925bf7af",
      "text" : "superfluous\n\n1. adj. 多余的；不必要的；奢侈的\n\n--- AI 释义 ---\n1）英\/ suːˈpɜːfluəs \/  美\/ suːˈpɜːrfluəs \/\n2）adj.多余的，过剩的，不必要的\n3）more than is needed or wanted; unnecessary\n4）But the due process clauses would be superfluous if all they did was to restate the protections of the Fourth,",
      "type" : "text",
      "width" : 260,
      "x" : 3124,
      "y" : 2664
    },
    {
      "color" : "6",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "24b14b4487981858",
      "text" : "obedience\n*obediences*\n\n1. n. 顺从；服从；遵守\n2. n. (Obedience)人名；(英)奥贝丁丝\n\n--- AI 释义 ---\n1）英\/ əˈbiːdiəns \/  美\/ oʊˈbiːdiəns \/\n2）\nn.服从，顺从；遵守，遵从\n3）the fact or condition of following orders, rules, or requests from someone in authority\n4）The soldiers were rewarded for their unquestioning obedience to their commander.",
      "type" : "text",
      "width" : 260,
      "x" : 3124,
      "y" : 2796
    },
    {
      "color" : "2",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "65081207619da258",
      "text" : "ratified\n*ratify*\n\n1. adj. 批准的\n2. vt. 批准（ratify的过去式）\n\n--- AI 释义 ---\n1）英\/ ˈrætɪfaɪd \/  美\/ ˈrætɪfaɪd \/\n2）\nv.正式批准，签署生效\n3）to formally approve or confirm something, usually by vote or official agreement\n4）The treaty was ratified by all participating nations after lengthy debates.",
      "type" : "text",
      "width" : 260,
      "x" : 3124,
      "y" : 2400
    },
    {
      "color" : "1",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "eccc3f7078ebc138",
      "text" : "seizure\n*seizures*\n\n1. n. 没收；夺取；捕获；（疾病的）突然发作\n\n--- AI 释义 ---\n1）英\/ ˈsiːʒə(r) \/  美\/ ˈsiːʒər \/\n2）\nn.  seizure（财产、物品等的）扣押，没收，查封；（疾病的）突然发作，阵发；（情感的）突然迸发；癫痫发作；夺取，占领\n3）the act of taking control of something, especially by force or legal authority\n4）The Fourth Amendment protects citizens against unreasonable searches and seizures.",
      "type" : "text",
      "width" : 260,
      "x" : 2776,
      "y" : 1740
    },
    {
      "color" : "2",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "aaf3c07b0a471365",
      "text" : "strike down\n\n1. na. 打倒；杀；(将鱼)装桶保藏；使生(病)\n2. [网络] 击倒；打翻；打垮",
      "type" : "text",
