    {
      "color" : "1",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "737f8135745851de",
      "text" : "constituents\n*constituent*\n\n1. n. 成分（constituent的复数）\n\n--- AI 释义 ---\n1）英\/ kənˈstɪtʃuənts \/  美\/ kənˈstɪtʃuənts \/\n2）\nn.选民，选区居民；成分，构成要素；组成成分；（机器的）组件\n3）the people who live and vote in a particular area, or the parts that form something\n4）The senator emphasized the importance of listening to his constituents before making a decision.",
      "type" : "text",
      "width" : 260,
      "x" : 2776,
      "y" : 816
    },
    {
      "color" : "1",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "348fac85e04d73af",
      "text" : "lobbied\n*lobby*\n\n1. vi. 为了支持或抵制某项特定目标游说（lobby的过去式与过去分词形式）\n\n--- AI 释义 ---\n1）英\/ ˈlɒbi \/  美\/ ˈlɑːbi \/\n2）\nv. 游说，对……进行疏通（以影响决策）；企图影响（议员、官员等）；（在议会走廊或休息室）游说议员\nn. 游说团体；门厅，大厅；议会休息室\n3）to try to persuade a politician, public official, or a government to support or oppose a particular action, law, or policy, especially by visiting them or writing to them\n4）The industry has lobbied the government to reduce taxes on their products.",
      "type" : "text",
      "width" : 260,
      "x" : 2504,
      "y" : 948
    },
    {
      "color" : "2",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "879dd1d5836de913",
      "text" : "pros and cons\n\n1. n. 利弊; 正反两方面; 优缺点; 赞成和反对的理由",
      "type" : "text",
      "width" : 260,
