      "y" : 2948
    },
    {
      "color" : "2",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "1e10b9c5f681c6a8",
      "text" : "immutable\n\n1）英\/ ɪˈmjuːtəbl \/  美\/ ɪˈmjuːtəbl \/\n2）adj.不可改变的，永恒不变的\n3）not subject or susceptible to change\n4）The law and legal decisions can be seen as inevitable, based on immutable principles of justice, hardly the product of human invention.\n\n--- 自定义笔记 ---\nim-（不）+ mut（变化）+ -able（可…的）→ 不可变化的。\n例句：The laws of physics are immutable, no matter how much we might wish otherwise. \n联想：想象一块刻着“物理定律”的巨石，无论风吹雨打、岁月流逝，它的形状和文字都纹丝不动——immutable 就是这种“雷打不动”的感觉。",
      "type" : "text",
      "width" : 260,
      "x" : 1304,
      "y" : 2684
    },
    {
      "color" : "2",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "d3196933035d8ea4",
      "text" : "off the hook\n\n1）英\/ɒf ðə hʊk\/  美\/ɔːf ðə hʊk\/\n2）\nadj.脱离困境的，脱身的；不再有责任的\n3）no longer in a difficult or responsible situation; free from an obligation or commitment that was previously required\n4）If you promise to take your children to the movies, are you off the hook if an important business meeting comes up?",
      "type" : "text",
      "width" : 260,
      "x" : 1304,
      "y" : 2420
    },
    {
      "color" : "2",
      "height" : 120,
      "id" : "a2f0a64051467747",
      "text" : "Pilgrims\n*pilgrim*\n\n1）英\/ ˈpɪlɡrɪmz \/  美\/ ˈpɪlɡrɪmz \/\n2）\nn.（尤指1620年到达美洲的）清教徒前辈移民；朝圣者；旅行者，流浪者\n3）members of a group of English Puritans who sailed to America on the Mayflower in 1620 and founded the Plymouth Colony in Massachusetts\n4）Even before the Pilgrims landed in Massachusetts, they had signed the Mayflower Compact to establish self-government.",
      "type" : "text",
      "width" : 260,
      "x" : 1576,
      "y" : 2420
    },
    {
      "color" : "2",
      "height" : 120,
